        "collapsible_tab_Kpnrzj": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Ingredient Descriptions",
            "icon": "eye",
            "content": "<p><a href=\"/blogs/ingredients/what-is-sodium-percarbonate\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"What is Sodium Percarbonate and what does it do in products?\"><strong>Sodium Percarbonate</strong></a><strong> </strong>(non-chlorine oxygen bleach, whitener)</p><p><a href=\"/blogs/ingredients/what-is-sodium-carbonate\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"What is Sodium Carbonate and what does it do in products?\"><strong>Sodium Carbonate</strong></a><strong> </strong>(washing soda, cleaner)</p><p><strong>Sodium Citrate</strong> (salt, prevents cloudiness)</p><p><a href=\"/blogs/ingredients/what-is-sodium-metasilicate\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"What is Sodium Metasilicate and what does it do in products?\"><strong>Sodium Metasilicate</strong></a> (salt, removes organic matter on dishes)</p><p><a href=\"/blogs/ingredients/what-is-sodium-chloride\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"What is Sodium Chloride and what does it do in products?\"><strong>Sodium Chloride</strong></a><strong> </strong>(salt, removes spots)</p><p><a href=\"/blogs/ingredients/what-is-sodium-gluconate\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"What is Sodium Gluconate and what does it do in products?\"><strong>Sodium Gluconate</strong></a><strong> </strong>(salt, reduces water tension)</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_EwVm9h": {
          "type": "collapsible_tab",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why does Rustic Strength’s natural dish detergent work differently than conventional brands?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "content": "<p>Rustic Strength automatic dish detergent is fundamentally different from conventional products, and that difference matters, especially in homes with hard water.</p><p>Most conventional dish detergents rely on <strong>synthetic surfactants, petroleum-derived chemicals, and artificial rinse aids.</strong> These ingredients are highly effective at binding minerals in hard water and facilitating their removal. The trade-off? <strong>Many of those chemicals are harsh on human health, waterways, septic systems, and indoor air quality.</strong></p><p><strong>Our detergent is made without those “extra nasty” chemicals</strong>, which means it cleans without leaving behind toxic residues on your dishes, but it also means it doesn’t overpower hard-water minerals the way conventional formulas do.</p><p>If you live in an area with hard water, the white spots or haze you sometimes see after a wash cycle are not detergent residue and not a film left behind by Rustic Strength’s products.</p><p>Those spots are:</p><ul><li>Calcium</li><li>Magnesium</li><li>Other naturally occurring minerals from your water supply</li></ul><p>During the final rinse cycle, as water evaporates, minerals from your home’s water supply are left behind on your dishes. Conventional detergents mask or chemically neutralize these minerals. Natural detergents don’t mask or neutralize these minerals.</p><p>In other words, our automatic dish powder did its job and cleaned your dishes! The minerals are simply left behind by your home’s water supply.</p><p>Our more natural dish detergent:</p><ul><li>Avoids dangerous synthetic cleaning agents</li><li>Uses milder, plant-based surfactants</li><li>Skips artificial coatings</li></ul>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
